Subtract \(b\) from both sides, then divide both sides by \(a\):
\[
\begin{aligned}
ax &= c-b\\
x &= \frac{c-b}{a}
\end{aligned}
\]
Therefore, the solution is \(x=\frac{c-b}{a}\).

Subtract \(2x\) from both sides, add \(3\) to both sides, then divide by \(3\):
\[
\begin{aligned}
a &= 3x-3\\
a+3 &= 3x\\
x &= \frac{a+3}{3}
\end{aligned}
\]
Therefore, the solution is \(x=\frac{a+3}{3}\).

Expand both sides, subtract \(bx\) from both sides, then add \(2a\) to both sides. Since \(a\ne b\), divide by \(a-b\):
\[
\begin{aligned}
ax-2a &= bx+b\\
ax-bx-2a &= b\\
(a-b)x &= 2a+b\\
x &= \frac{2a+b}{a-b}
\end{aligned}
\]
Therefore, the solution is \(x=\frac{2a+b}{a-b}\).
